    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        0,
        1120
      ],
      "size": [
        900,
        380
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 32,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Add sound to a video\n\n1. Load a clip in **Silent video**. Any clip works; whatever sound it has is replaced.\n2. Describe what should be heard in **Sounds**: materials, actions, surroundings. End with \"No speech is present. No music is present.\", which is how the LoRA was trained.\n3. Run. The video keeps its own frames and frame rate; the new track is generated to match the picture.\n\nThe picture is only encoded so the model can see it, at 768 px on the long side. Raising that makes the run slower without changing the output frames. Frame counts are rounded down to 1 + a multiple of 8, so up to seven frames can drop from the end."
      ],
      "title": "How to use"
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        460,
        1120
      ],
      "size": [
        900,
        460
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 33,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## About this workflow\n\nThe recipe and prompts come from RuneXX's `LTX-2.3_-_V2V_Foley_Add_Sound_To_Any_Video_Foley-Lora.json` in [RuneXX/LTX-2.3-Workflows](https://huggingface.co/RuneXX/LTX-2.3-Workflows) (Video-2-Video folder). The LoRA is Lightricks' [LTX-2.3 Foley V2A](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.3-22b-LoRA-Foley-V2A).\n\nRebuilt for this repo on core nodes and the LTX-2.5 distilled stack:\n- LTX-2.5 distilled transformer (comfy-int8-convrot, 21.5 GB) and its Gemma 4 12B int8 encoder instead of LTX-2.3 dev with the distilled LoRA at 0.4. The NVFP4 transformer (18.7 GB) loads too.\n- The 8-step distilled schedule from Lightricks' 2.5 graphs instead of 30 dev steps. RuneXX recommends dev at 30 steps on 2.3; LTX-2.5 runs most 2.3 LoRAs, so this uses what the repo already provisions.\n- The video is frozen with a zero noise mask before it joins the audio latent, the mirror of how Lightricks' audio to video graph freezes audio. RuneXX's graph does the same with `LTXVSetAudioVideoMaskByTime`.\n- No GGUF branch, sampler-preview, attention-patch, rgthree or Video Helper Suite nodes. KJNodes is used for one resize.\n- Sample clip `white_armored_warrior.mp4` from Comfy's template inputs, with a prompt written for it.\n\nAsset profile: `ltx-2.5-foley`."
      ],
      "title": "About this workflow"
    }
